VibeGo changes: correct ED 1/3 semantics and provide independent screen
scrollback configuration; erase complete wide glyphs with the active background.
Saved cursor state also retains pending autowrap across restore/alternate-screen exit.
ANSI CSI u restores the cursor saved by CSI s.
Origin-mode changes home the cursor; HVP uses the same origin as CUP.
Relative cursor movement respects the opposite margin when starting outside a region.
DECSTR restores input defaults without erasing the screen or switching buffers.
ANSI insert mode shifts existing cells before printable glyphs are written.
Wide glyphs wrap before overflow and retain pending wrap when filling the right edge.
Zero-width combining clusters in subsequent writes attach to the preceding glyph.
Same-width emoji modifiers and ZWJ continuations rejoin across Write boundaries.
Growing grapheme clusters update cell width and wrap position when later selectors arrive.
Cell insertion preserves shifted wide glyphs and clears split push-off boundaries.
Cell deletion moves intact wide glyphs without destructive per-cell rewrites.
Pending grapheme buffers and projected cell graphemes are bounded to 256 bytes;
excess combining content is dropped from the screen projection, not raw recording.
Control strings exceeding 4 MiB are rejected as a whole rather than dispatched
with silently truncated payloads; one sentinel byte detects parser overflow.
Right-margin attachment is retained with autowrap disabled; growing selectors
without room are rejected without erasing the narrow base or its neighbors.
Saved cursors in both buffers are mapped and bounded when the screen resizes,
including the logical position represented by a saved right-margin state.
Legacy DEC mode 47 and mode 1047 switch buffers without implicitly saving,
restoring or homing the cursor; repeated activation does not clear content.
DECRQM for alternate-screen selectors reports the actual active buffer even
when programs enter and leave using different selectors.
An opaque in-memory checkpoint captures independent screen/continuation state
at complete parser boundaries, preserving target I/O and handlers on restore.
Versioned JSON checkpoint encoding retains typed colors and validates imported
geometry, cells, modes and resource limits without modifying a live emulator.
No Warp source code is included in this module.
Saved cursors independently retain all four graphic character sets and shift
selection. SI/SO and seven-bit single shifts dispatch through working handlers.
Version 2 checkpoints persist saved character state; legacy version 1 imports
retain explicitly unknown saved character state rather than inventing it.
Graphic character mapping precedes grapheme joining and wrapping, preserving
combining marks and repeat state across arbitrary Write boundaries.
Version 3 checkpoints preserve explicit soft-wrap layout through row movement,
scrollback and snapshots. Legacy or unsupported reflow layouts remain unknown.
ED 2 erases the viewport in place with its erase background, matching the
browser terminal rather than appending duplicate history.
